; reduce_charge_before_index_check: REDUCE is charged its four entries and
; one variable before its index is range-checked, so an exhausted budget
; decides the fault.
;
; spec/xqvm/SPEC.md orders the work within one instruction: pops, then the
; allocation charge, then validation, and charges a coefficient write on a
; model register ("Charging points and counting units"). The model below is
; four binary variables (32 bytes at the variable rate) under a budget of
; exactly 32, so any further charge is refused. Index 9 is out of range, so
; with budget to spare this instruction raises IndexOutOfBounds; with none
; the charge comes first and decides the fault.
;
; The fault-ordering table in this directory's README once listed this
; opcode as pinned by xqvm_py's unit tests alone.

PUSH 4
BQMX r0          ; 32 bytes: the whole budget
PUSH 9           ; var_a, out of range [0, 4)
PUSH 0           ; var_b
PUSH 1           ; P_aux
REDUCE r0
HALT
